## Canonical Reasoning Cycle (B.5)

| Phase | Name | Core Question | FPF Alignment |
|-------|------|---------------|---------------|
| **Abduction** | Propose | "Most plausible explanation?" | Creates L0 artifact |
| **Deduction** | Analyze | "If true, what follows?" | Verification Assurance (VA) |
| **Induction** | Test | "Do predictions match reality?" | Validation Assurance (LA) |

Agent workflow: OBSERVE → SEARCH → LOAD → PLAN → EXECUTE → AUDIT.

## Core Terminology

Answer term-only questions from these tables without loading files.

### Ontological Core (Part A)

| Term | Pattern | Definition |
|------|---------|------------|
| **Holon** | A.1 | Entity that is simultaneously a whole AND a part. |
| **BoundedContext** | A.1.1 | Semantic frame where terms have meaning. Meaning is LOCAL. |
| **System** | A.1 | Physical/digital entity that can bear roles and execute work. |
| **Role** | A.2 | A mask/identity that a System wears. Role ≠ behavior. |
| **MethodDescription** | A.3.2 | Design-time recipe. NOT execution. |
| **Work** | A.15.1 | Run-time occurrence. Dated, consumes resources. IMMUTABLE. |
| **Transformer** | A.12 | Agent: input → output. External = tool. Reflexive = self-mod. |
| **Episteme** | A.0 | Knowledge artifact with carriers (files, models, beliefs). |

### Core Principles (Part A)

| Principle | Pattern | Definition |
|-----------|---------|------------|
| **Strict Distinction** | A.7 | Map ≠ Territory. Plan ≠ execution. |
| **Evidence Graph** | A.10 | All claims need auditable evidence chains. |
| **Ontological Parsimony** | A.11 | Do not multiply entities beyond necessity. |
| **Cross-Scale Consistency** | A.9 | Rules apply at all scales. |

### Reasoning (Part B)

| Term | Pattern | Definition |
|------|---------|------------|
| **Aggregation (Gamma)** | B.1 | How parts combine into wholes. Gamma_sys, Gamma_epist, Gamma_work. |
| **Trust Calculus (F-G-R)** | B.3 | Formality, Granularity/Scope, Reliability. |
| **Canonical Evolution Loop** | B.4 | OBSERVE → REFINE → DEPLOY → AUDIT. |
| **Canonical Reasoning Cycle** | B.5 | Abduction → Deduction → Induction. |

